# docs/ is NOT ignored, on purpose.
#
# It is build output, so the instinct is to ignore it and let the host run
# `node tools/build_www.js`. Two reasons not to:
#
#   1. package.json declares Capacitor, so a host that auto-installs would pull
#      ~29MB of Android tooling to serve a static site, and any hiccup there
#      fails the deploy.
#   2. Committing the build means the bytes that go live are exactly the ones
#      tools/pwa_check.js verified — no build environment in between that
#      nobody has tested.
#
# So the deploy has NO build step. GitHub Pages serves docs/ on main directly;
# that folder is named docs/ and not www/ only because Pages will serve a
# branch's root or its /docs and nothing else. Run `node tools/build_www.js`
# before committing; it stamps sw.js with a content hash, so the cache busts
# itself.
